{
  "name": "VO Capture & Control · MASTER (All-in-One)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## VO Capture & Control — all-in-one workflow\n\n**Client:** `MASTER` (template — this copy runs nothing)\n**App:** `https://vo.osmanflow.com`\n\nOne file, one import, every lane. Node names carry their lane letter so a\nfailed execution names the lane before anything has to be opened.\n\n### Before this file is a client's workflow — the duplication checklist\n\n1. **Rebind every credential.** Gmail, Google Drive. Credentials do NOT travel\n   with an export; the fields look filled and are not.\n2. **Regenerate every webhook path.** Two clients sharing `vo/whatsapp` means\n   one contractor's site photos land in another contractor's register.\n3. **Set the environment on the n8n container** (`docker compose` env, not this\n   file — the repo is public and a secret in here is a published secret):\n   `VO_APP_URL`, `VO_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `VO_OUTBOUND_SECRET`,\n   `VO_EVOLUTION_URL`, `VO_EVOLUTION_INSTANCE`, `VO_EVOLUTION_API_KEY`.\n4. **Point Evolution's webhook** at lane A's production URL, event\n   `MESSAGES_UPSERT` only.\n5. **Import deactivated. Test each lane. Then activate.**\n\n⚠️ Activation is all-or-nothing — that is the cost of one file per client.\nLane H routes failures by letter so the cost is bearable.",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky0",
      "name": "Note 0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1560,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## How a request is signed, and why it is fussy\n\nEvery call to the app carries `x-vo-timestamp` and `x-vo-signature`, an\nHMAC-SHA256 over the string `timestamp.rawBody` — the exact bytes, not the\nobject.\n\n**So the body is sent as `raw`, never as `json`.** If the HTTP node were left\non JSON body it would re-serialise the object, key order and spacing could\ndiffer by one byte from what was hashed, and every request would fail\nverification with a message about the signature that says nothing about the\ncause. The Code node builds the string; the Crypto node signs that string; the\nHTTP node sends that same string.\n\n**The secret is `$env.VO_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, never typed into a node.** A secret in\na parameter is a secret in the exported JSON, and this file lives in a public\nrepository.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "sticky1",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1560,
        440
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Lane A · WhatsApp in (Evolution)\n**Trigger:** Evolution posts `MESSAGES_UPSERT` here.\n**Calls:** `POST /api/integrations/whatsapp/incoming-message`\n**Idempotency:** `evolution:<message id>` — Evolution retries, and a retry must\nnot create a second Potential Change.\n\n**This lane must never:** decide which project a message belongs to. It carries\nthe sender's phone; the app resolves identity and memberships. A courier that\nguesses at a project is how a claim ends up on the wrong job.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "sticky2",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -880,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "vo/whatsapp",
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "responseData": "firstEntryJson",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "n003-a1",
      "name": "A1 · Webhook: WhatsApp In",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        -300,
        -300
      ],
      "webhookId": "vo-whatsapp"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Evolution speaks Baileys. The app speaks its own contract. This is the only\n// node that knows both, on purpose: when Evolution changes shape, one node\n// changes.\nconst body = $json.body ?? $json;\nconst data = body.data ?? {};\nconst key = data.key ?? {};\n\n// Our own outgoing messages come back through the same event.\nif (key.fromMe) return [];\n\nconst m = data.message ?? {};\nconst text = m.conversation ?? m.extendedTextMessage?.text ?? '';\nconst caption = m.imageMessage?.caption ?? m.videoMessage?.caption\n  ?? m.documentMessage?.caption ?? '';\n\nlet type = 'text';\nif (m.imageMessage) type = 'image';\nelse if (m.audioMessage) type = 'audio';\nelse if (m.videoMessage) type = 'video';\nelse if (m.documentMessage) type = 'document';\n\n// Nothing to read and nothing to look at. Not an error, just not a change.\nif (!text && !caption && type === 'text') return [];\n\nconst jid = String(key.remoteJid ?? '');\n// Groups end @g.us and carry the real sender in `participant`. A group message\n// signed by the group would resolve to no user at all.\nconst sender = jid.endsWith('@g.us') ? String(key.participant ?? '') : jid;\n\nconst payload = {\n  idempotency_key: 'evolution:' + (key.id ?? ''),\n  received_at: new Date((Number(data.messageTimestamp) || Date.now() / 1000) * 1000).toISOString(),\n  sender: {\n    phone: '+' + sender.split('@')[0].split(':')[0],\n    display_name: data.pushName || undefined,\n  },\n  message: {\n    type,\n    text: text || undefined,\n    caption: caption || undefined,\n    media: [],\n  },\n};\n\nreturn [{ json: { ts: String(Date.now()), payload: JSON.stringify(payload) } }];"
      },
      "id": "n004-a2",
      "name": "A2 · Shape Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "action": "hmac",
        "type": "SHA256",
        "value": "={{ $json.ts + '.' + $json.payload }}",
        "dataPropertyName": "signature",
        "secret": "={{ $env.VO_WEBHOOK_SECRET }}",
        "encoding": "hex"
      },
      "id": "n005-a3",
      "name": "A3 · Sign",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.crypto",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        140,
        -300
