    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Lane D · Email out\n**Trigger:** the app posts a queued notification here.\n**Sends:** Gmail.\n**Then:** reports back to `/api/integrations/notifications/delivery-status`.\n\n**The callback is the point.** The app marks a row `queued` when it hands the\nmessage over, never `sent`. Only D9 can move it to delivered. Without that,\nthe app would claim a notice was delivered on the strength of its own outbound\nrequest — which is exactly the claim that loses an argument later.\n\n**Bound to the `Gmail account` credential.**",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "sticky17",
      "name": "Note 17",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -880,
        520
      ]
